WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.122
Let’s finish with the full workflow.

00:00:02.122 --> 00:00:05.507
Read the data. Separate features and target.

00:00:05.507 --> 00:00:10.067
Split before evaluation. Train a model on the training set.

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:12.947
Evaluate on unseen test rows.

00:00:12.947 --> 00:00:15.412
Compare performance with a baseline.

00:00:15.412 --> 00:00:19.059
Make new predictions carefully, and watch for leakage.

00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:24.005
You now have a first end-to-end machine learning workflow in Python.

00:00:24.005 --> 00:00:32.710
The next step in a dedicated machine learning course would be deeper work on preprocessing, model selection, validation,

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:36.461
metrics, tuning, and responsible deployment.

00:00:36.916 --> 00:00:42.833
This is the final module in the course, so there is not another numbered module after this one.

00:00:42.833 --> 00:00:50.828
The next step is to bring the full workflow together in your own analytics work: obtain data, prepare it carefully,

00:00:50.828 --> 00:00:58.923
explore it, summarize it, communicate what you find, and use predictive methods only when they fit the question.

00:00:58.923 --> 00:01:05.928
The goal is not simply to know individual Python commands, but to be able to choose and connect the right methods for a

00:01:05.928 --> 00:01:07.628
complete analytical problem.
